7. Account API DTOs and Validation

AccountRequest accepts only fields the caller is allowed to control:

customerId   -> @NotNull + @Positive

accountType  -> @NotNull

The client does not supply accountNumber, balance, accountStatus, createdAt, or updatedAt. Those values are system controlled.

AccountResponse returns:

accountId, accountNumber, customerId, accountType,

balance, accountStatus, createdAt, updatedAt

8. Oracle-Generated Account Number

ACCOUNT_NUMBER is generated in Oracle rather than Java. A sequence and trigger produce a fixed-width 10-digit business identifier.

ACCOUNT_NUMBER_SEQ

TRG_ACCOUNTS_NUMBER


Example:

0000000001

0000000002

After saveAndFlush(), EntityManager.refresh() reloads the trigger-generated account number into the JPA entity before the API response is returned.

9. Flyway Migration Strategy

Migration

Purpose

V1__create_account_schema.sql

Create ACCOUNTS, indexes, sequence, trigger and check constraints

V2__add_unique_customer_account_type.sql

Prevent duplicate account type for the same customer

Because Customer Service and Account Service currently share FINANCIAL_USER locally, Account Service uses its own Flyway history table.

spring.flyway.table=account_flyway_schema_history

spring.flyway.baseline-on-migrate=true

spring.flyway.baseline-version=0

The baseline at version 0 allows Account Service V1 to run even though the shared local Oracle schema already contains Customer Service objects. Flyway history was verified with baseline 0 and successful migration 1.

Future AWS deployment can package approved SQL through CI/CD and S3. S3 is storage, not a migration executor; a deployment job must still execute the scripts.

