18. Engineering Lessons

Separate technical IDs from business-facing numbers.

Do not create JPA relationships across microservice domain boundaries.

Application validation improves user feedback; database constraints provide final integrity.

Schema migrations must have isolated history when multiple services share a local schema.

A CLOSED financial account should be treated as a terminal lifecycle state unless a dedicated controlled process says otherwise.

Balance should not become a generic client-editable field; future Transaction Service will own controlled money movement.

Local shared Oracle is a development convenience, not the final production data-isolation model.

19. Next Development Step

Implement Account Service -> Customer Service validation so an account can only be created for a real, ACTIVE customer. After that, the project can continue toward richer account operations and the Transaction Service.

